    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive strategy for today, 2026-08-08, pivots heavily on exploiting favorable matchups against secondary arms while mitigating the impact of elite pitching. **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Andy Pages** (72.12) anchor our daily efficiency rankings, benefitting significantly from a high-upside matchup against Brandon Pfaadt. **Pages** in particular sees a boost from his ability to exploit a slow delivery, providing a clear path to stolen bases\u2014a critical priority for our roster construction. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (72.17) offers a premium start against Jake Bennett, where a combination of park factors and a prime #2 spot in the lineup elevates his output well above his base projection. While **Gunnar Henderson** (61.80) faces the daunting task of squaring off against Jacob deGrom, his projected volume and batting order position provide enough stability to warrant a start despite the elite SP hurdle.\n\nThe optimization process resulted in a tight decision regarding **Dominic Smith** (46.69), who narrowly missed the final cut for our UTIL slot. While **Dominic Smith** offers solid structural value, **Luis Robert Jr.** (62.18) was ultimately preferred despite a platoon disadvantage because of his superior speed profile against Bubba Chandler; the opportunity for stolen bases against a favorable matchup ultimately tipped the scales. We remain cautious regarding **Heliot Ramos** (49.09), who faces the elite Chris Sale; his score is suppressed by a significant SP skill penalty, placing him at the bottom of our recommended starters. Furthermore, users should note that all projections are predicated on pending lineups; any shifts in batting order for **Liam Hicks** or **Drake Baldwin** could impact their efficiency ratings, particularly if they are moved further down the lineup away from high-RBI opportunities.",
